[Music]  hi my name is yufeng guo and today we're  going to look at how tensorflow  enterprise or tfe  builds on tensorflow to enable the  seamless creation of production machine  learning applications with  enterprise-grade support  through the power of google cloud to  learn about the benefits of tfe let's  imagine a scenario where a data  scientist visits an ops team to ask for  help productionizing their machine  learning platform  the question then becomes whether there  is a suitable platform for both  experimentation and production  tensorflow enterprise is ideal for this  kind of situation  google cloud has your solution to  productionize your tensorflow  applications  as part of google cloud tfe provides  managed services  cloud scale performance and enterprise  grade support  let's start with managed services and  check back in to see how our data  science and ops teams are doing  the data science team needs development  environments with lots of compute power  and in an on-prem non-managed system the  burden of setting them up often falls to  the ops team  [Music]  there are many challenges to operating  this way machines with gpus are  expensive and take a long time to  acquire  software installation and management  consume significant time  additionally there's the problem of over  provisioning  this kind of non-managed ml platform  doesn't scale for enterprise production  projects  one solution to these constraints is to  introduce a standardized ml platform for  the data scientists and ops teams  to solve these problems enter tensorflow  enterprise on the deep learning vm  or dlvm the dlvm is a standardized  vm image for machine learning  applications tfe currently supports  tensorflow 1.15 and  2. the machine comes pre-installed with  the everyday tools for data scientists  including cuda drivers numpy sklearn  pandas and of course jupiter  since it's a standardized software stack  it's easily manageable by ops engineers  the dlvm is deployable to google cloud  with google compute engine or ai  platform notebooks  in just a few minutes also there's no  over provisioning problem because you  only pay for the resources you actually  use  minute by minute let's take a look at  how you can actually create a gce  instance with the dlvm image in the gcp  console head on over to the compute  engine's vm instances page and click  create select marketplace from the left  hand menu and type deep learning vm in  the search bar  select the deep learning vm and click  launch in this menu you can select your  machine type and if you want gpus  you can also select the tensorflow  enterprise versions 1.15  and 2. for now let's choose tensorflow  1.15 without gpus  and just one cpu a very simple image and  just click  deploy the manageability you just saw  increases the portability and  scalability that you just can't get  with local notebooks there's often a  huge gap between  proof of concept notebooks and  production machine learning code  for example notebooks are often  particular to the local environment of  each data scientist  but production code should be portable  and shareable  a single notebook instance can't serve  10 million users  the ops teams have to take on a lot of  work to scale and load balance to build  a production system  proof of concepts are manually deployed  whereas in production the ops team needs  to manage a reproducible end-to-end  life cycle and after all of that  continuous monitoring and alerting still  need to be taken into consideration  one way to fill the gap between  experimentation and production  is deep learning containers or dlc with  tensorflow enterprise  dlc provides the exact same standardized  ml software stack as a dlvm  with support for tensorflow 1.15 and 2  as well as lots of common data science  libraries but now it's on a portable and  scalable container image  if your data science team is already  using dlvms then it's much easier for  ops engineers to migrate their code to  dlc and deploy it to google cloud  services such as ai platform and  kubernetes engine  with deep learning containers the ops  team won't have to add a hundred  thousand lines of code to make a robust  system for example if you use ai  platform or kubernetes engine to run the  container  you automatically get the benefits from  the managed service such as container  scheduling and lifecycle management  scaling out to load balancing and  failover logging and monitoring  troubleshooting security and more  now let's see how scale cloud  performance of tensorflow enterprise can  benefit you  in many cases data scientists tend to  use smaller sample data sets for  building their machine learning models  and don't bother handling the raw big  data so  it falls to the ops team to design an ml  pipeline that can accommodate the 10  million rows from storage without any i  o bottleneck  and continuously and smoothly  pre-process and train the model  every day because tensorflow enterprise  provides tensorflow runtimes  specifically designed for google cloud  you can fully utilize the cloud scale  performance of both cloud storage  and bigquery with minimal changes to  your existing tensorflow code  lastly let's talk about enterprise grade  support the pace of ai and software  versions is evolving  rapidly and it's hard to keep up with  new library versions always coming out  that is why tensorflow enterprise  includes long-term support  for tensorflow 1.15 and 2 google cloud  will provide security patches and select  bug fixes for up to  3 years these versions will be available  on google cloud and all patches and bug  fixes will also be available  in the mainline tensorflow repository  tensorflow enterprise is available today  with support for tensorflow 1.15 and 2.  speed up your software development and  ensure the longevity and reliability of  your ai applications and services  with enterprise grade support it's the  only offering  from the same team that created  tensorflow head over to g dot co  cloud tensorflow to get started today

